<h3 class="storytitle" id="post-13"><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/blog/index.php?p=13" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Nothing in particular">Nothing in particular</a></h3>
<!-- Post meta -->
<div class="meta">
Posted on May 25th, 2004. <!-- By Mark. --> About <a href="http://www.marksportal.net/blog/index.php?cat=1" title="View all posts in General">General</a>. <a href="http://www.marksportal.net/blog/index.php?p=13#comments">No Comments</a>.</div>

<!-- Actual post -->
<div class="storycontent">
	<p>I was reminded recently how much I enjoyed the movie <a href="http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0181875/"> &#8220;Almost Famous&#8221;</a>.  I&#8217;m not sure why but it seem to really resonate with me.  Maybe resonate isn&#8217;t the right word, but it sounds like it is.  <a href="http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0117998/"> &#8220;Twister&#8221;</a> did the same thing for me.  I really am not sure why I enjoyed these two movies so much, yet there was just something to them that seemed to touch my heart.  They were &#8220;feel good&#8221; movies for me that left my heart aching.  Whether that&#8217;s bad or good I can&#8217;t say, but that aching can sure act like an addictive drug sometimes. <img src='http://www.marksportal.net/blog/wp-images/smilies/icon_wink.gif' alt=';)' class='wp-smiley' />   </p>
	<p>Remember when I talked about &#8220;signs&#8221; in a previous post?  Well, today I recieved more signs that were contrary to the first ones.   I think I&#8217;m reading into these &#8220;signs&#8221; a bit too much.  I guess it&#8217;s human nature.  When we want something bad enough everything we see becomes associated with that thing.   I haven&#8217;t decided yet whether I am going to go through with this thing I&#8217;m nervous/scared of doing.   What a chicken I am! <img src='http://www.marksportal.net/blog/wp-images/smilies/icon_wink.gif' alt=';)' class='wp-smiley' /> </p>
</div>			
