<h3 class="storytitle" id="post-11"><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/blog/index.php?p=11" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Good intentions">Good intentions</a></h3>
<!-- Post meta -->
<div class="meta">
Posted on May 23rd, 2004. <!-- By Mark. --> About <a href="http://www.marksportal.net/blog/index.php?cat=3" title="View all posts in The Narrow Path">The Narrow Path</a>. <a href="http://www.marksportal.net/blog/index.php?p=11#comments">No Comments</a>.</div>

<!-- Actual post -->
<div class="storycontent">
	<p>There&#8217;s been a lot of things that I&#8217;ve wanted to write about these last couple of days, but when I&#8217;ve finally found the time to sit down and write, it&#8217;s seemed a bit overwhelming.   So now, everythings been piled up and I&#8217;m not sure what to mention and what not to. </p>
	<p>My cousin took a bad fall off a cliff and is now in a coma.  It&#8217;s interesting that in times of trouble people turn to God for help, yet during times of peace we barely speak to Him.  I&#8217;m sure God is used to it by now, though not pleased.  This sort of behavior is seen all over in the Old Testament, so it&#8217;s nothing that&#8217;s new.   I&#8217;m reminded of this verse:</p>
	<p><em>&#8220;Remember also your Creator in the days of your youth, before the evil days come&#8230; &#8221; </em>(Ecclesiastes 12:1, NASB95) </p>
	<p>Though it says &#8220;days of your youth&#8221;, I believe it also applies to days of prosperity as well.   A day before I was informed of the accident I had a friend ask me if I thought we could &#8220;move mountains&#8221; like Jesus said we could do if we had faith (<a href="http://bible1.crosswalk.com/OnlineStudyBible/bible.cgi?passage=mt+17:20">Matthew 17:20</a>).   I answered that I thought we could if the Trinity was in agreement.  I find it interesting that the very next day I learn of my cousin&#8217;s condition.   So I went before God and asked Him to bring my cousin out of the coma and heal him.   I&#8217;m convienced that God heard my prayer,  but I&#8217;m still uncertain of how He will answer.   Then again, maybe He has already given me an answer but am unable to perceive it.  </p>
	<p>My thoughts are scattered right now so I think I&#8217;ll just end this.</p>
